title: 'Studio Recipe + parametric cuts + editable captions — Phase 2 value play formalized'
summary: 'Multi-turn strategic session crystallized the Atelier "value play" for UGC: ship a system where content style (silence-trim feel, word-by-word caption highlights, overlay rhythm, transitions, palette, fonts) is captured as a reusable, shareable Studio Recipe — extractable from any reference video and re-appliable to fresh footage by the Composer agent (Iris). This converts Atelier from "yet another editor" into "style-as-a-preset" infrastructure. Three new content-generation agents added to the a-paradigm roster on 2026-05-12 (Quill the Showrunner, Lux the Cinematographer, Iris the Composer) form the word→image→composition pipeline that executes this play. Locked two foundational architectural decisions for the implementation phase: (1) the parametric-cut model — every detected boundary is immutable, padding is user-tunable, re-runs preserve overrides; (2) the layer-tagging convention — each pipeline owns its own tag namespace (silence-trim, caption, caption-word, overlay), and re-runs never touch other pipelines'' layers. Same pattern (detected-vs-user-edited, preserve through re-runs) applies to transcript edits — fix a misheard word, re-transcribe, your fix survives. Two specs landed: .paradigm/specs/silence-trim.md (parametric cuts + atelier trim CLI, T-007b) and .paradigm/specs/captions.md (Whisper transcribe + editable transcript + caption layer generation, T-006). Both with zero or one new npm dep, library vetting included, no critical issues found.'
